_at":"2026-10-05T15:59:33Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: Godot v4.7.stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 - Godot v4.7.stable - Vulkan (Mobile) - Intel HD Graphics 620 - Intel Core I5-7200U\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the Mobile renderer, AreaLight3D shows a black curved artifact when looking at it from the front.\n\nThe artifact follows the AreaLight3D when it is moved and disappears immediately when the AreaLight3D is removed or out of view.\n\nThe artifact does not affect the actual lighting of objects. Objects placed inside the black area are lit normally.\n\nThis issue only occurs with the Mobile renderer. It does not occur with the Forward+ or Compatibility renderers.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new 3D scene in Godot.\n2. Add a PlaneMesh (or any flat surface) to the scene.\n3. Add an AreaLight3D node.\n4. Set the project renderer to Mobile.\n5. Run the project.\n6. Look directly at the AreaLight3D from the front.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Hi.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29476763/Hi.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":